IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sa-nouns`

-- Part 4 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): commencement, amendment, replacement, repeal and expiry.
-- Sections 27 (commencement of Acts), 28 (time of commencement) and 30 (time of expiry) are time rules and are encoded in
-- sa-interpretation-time.l4; this module encodes sections 29 and 31 to 34.

§ `Part 4 -- Commencement, amendment, replacement, repeal and expiry (sections 29 and 31 to 34)`

§§ `29 -- Expiry`

-- src:393 | An Act or a legislative instrument may include a provision specifying a day on which the Act or instrument (or any provision of the Act or instrument) expires.
@ref s 29 (src:393)
`an Act or legislative instrument may include a provision specifying a day on which it expires` MEANS JUST TRUE

§§ `31 -- Use of headings to indicate amending provisions`

DECLARE `Heading that refers to an amendment` IS ONE OF
    `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified Act`
    `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by the same authority`
    `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by another authority`

-- src:397 | (1) In an Act, a provision under a heading referring to the amendment of a specified Act or a legislative instrument amends the Act or instrument so specified.
-- src:398 | (2) In a legislative instrument made by an authority, a provision under a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by the same authority amends the instrument so specified.
@ref s 31 (src:397-398)
GIVEN `where the provision is` IS A `Kind of enactment`
      `the heading it is under` IS A `Heading that refers to an amendment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a provision under a heading amends what the heading specifies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the provision is`
        WHEN `an Act` THEN
            CONSIDER `the heading it is under`
                WHEN `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified Act` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by the same authority` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by another authority` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a legislative instrument` THEN
            CONSIDER `the heading it is under`
                WHEN `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified Act` THEN NOTHING
                WHEN `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by the same authority` THEN JUST TRUE
                WHEN `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by another authority` THEN NOTHING

§§ `32 -- Effect of repeal, amendment or expiry`

DECLARE `Thing a repeal, amendment or expiry might touch` IS ONE OF
    `reviving anything not in force or existing at that time`
    `the previous operation of the Act, instrument or provision, or anything duly done or suffered under it`
    `any direct amendments made by the Act, instrument or provision`
    `a right, interest, title, power or privilege created, acquired, accrued, established or exercisable, or a status or capacity existing, under it`
    `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, imposed, created or incurred, or liable to be, under it`
    `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right or such a duty or penalty`
    `something else a repeal, amendment or expiry might touch`

-- src:400 | (1) This section applies if an Act or a legislative instrument, or a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument—
-- src:401 | (a) is repealed or amended; or
-- src:402 | (b) expires.
-- src:403 | (2) The repeal, amendment or expiry of the Act, legislative instrument or provision does not—
-- src:404 | (a) revive anything not in force or existing at that time; or
-- src:405 | (b) affect the previous operation of the Act, instrument or provision or anything duly done or suffered under it; or
-- src:406 | (c) affect any direct amendments made by the Act, instrument or provision; or
-- src:407 | (d) affect any right, interest, title, power or privilege created, acquired, accrued, established or exercisable, or any status or capacity existing, under the Act, instrument or provision; or
-- src:408 | (e) affect any duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof imposed, created or incurred, or any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred or imposed or liable to be incurred or imposed, under the Act, instrument or provision; or
-- src:409 | (f) affect any investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of anything mentioned in paragraph (d) or (e).
@ref s 32(1) and (2) (src:400-409)
GIVEN `the Act, instrument or provision has been repealed or amended, or has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `Thing a repeal, amendment or expiry might touch`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Act, instrument or provision has been repealed or amended, or has expired`) THEN NOTHING
    ELSE (CONSIDER thing
            WHEN `reviving anything not in force or existing at that time` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `the previous operation of the Act, instrument or provision, or anything duly done or suffered under it` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `any direct amendments made by the Act, instrument or provision` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `a right, interest, title, power or privilege created, acquired, accrued, established or exercisable, or a status or capacity existing, under it` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, imposed, created or incurred, or liable to be, under it` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right or such a duty or penalty` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `something else a repeal, amendment or expiry might touch` THEN NOTHING)

DECLARE `Proceeding or penalty after a repeal` IS ONE OF
    `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy mentioned in section 32(2)(f)`
    `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment mentioned in section 32(2)(e)`
    `any other proceeding or penalty`

-- src:410 | (3) An investigation, legal proceeding or remedy mentioned in subsection (2)(f) may be commenced, continued or enforced, and a penalty, forfeiture or punishment mentioned in subsection (2)(e) may be imposed, as if the Act, legislative instrument or provision had not been repealed or amended or had not expired.
@ref s 32(3) (src:410)
GIVEN thing IS A `Proceeding or penalty after a repeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it may be commenced, continued, enforced or imposed as if the Act had not been repealed, amended or expired` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy mentioned in section 32(2)(f)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment mentioned in section 32(2)(e)` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `any other proceeding or penalty` THEN NOTHING

-- src:411 | (4) If an office, court, tribunal or body would, apart from this section, cease to exist by reason of the repeal, amendment or expiry, then, for the purpose of instituting, continuing or enforcing any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy, the office, court, tribunal or body continues in existence (and, if necessary, new appointments may be made to it) as if the repeal or amendment had not been effected, or as if the expired Act, legislative instrument or provision had not expired (as the case may be).
@ref s 32(4) (src:411)
GIVEN `the office, court, tribunal or body would, apart from section 32, cease to exist by reason of the repeal, amendment or expiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is instituting, continuing or enforcing an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the office, court, tribunal or body continues in existence` MEANS
    IF `the office, court, tribunal or body would, apart from section 32, cease to exist by reason of the repeal, amendment or expiry`
    THEN (IF `the purpose is instituting, continuing or enforcing an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:412 | (5) An Act or a legislative instrument, or a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, will, despite its repeal, amendment or expiry, continue in force for the purposes of continuing and completing any act, matter or thing commenced or in progress under that Act, instrument or provision if there is no substituted Act, instrument or provision adapted to its continuance and completion.
@ref s 32(5) (src:412)
GIVEN `an act, matter or thing was commenced or in progress under the Act, instrument or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a substituted Act, instrument or provision adapted to its continuance and completion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the repealed, amended or expired provision continues in force for completing the act, matter or thing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is a substituted Act, instrument or provision adapted to its continuance and completion` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `an act, matter or thing was commenced or in progress under the Act, instrument or provision` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Thing section 32(6) protects` IS ONE OF
    `the continued operation of a provision of a savings or transitional nature enacted or made by the Act, instrument or provision`
    `the validating effect of a provision enacted or made by the Act, instrument or provision that validates anything that is or may otherwise be invalid`
    `something else section 32(6) protects`

-- src:413 | (6) The repeal, amendment or expiry of the Act, legislative instrument or provision does not—
-- src:414 | (a) affect the continued operation of a provision enacted or made by that Act, instrument or provision that is of a savings or transitional nature; or
-- src:415 | (b) end the validating effect of a provision enacted or made by that Act, instrument or provision that validates anything that is or may otherwise be invalid.
@ref s 32(6) (src:413-415)
GIVEN `the Act, instrument or provision has been repealed or amended, or has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `Thing section 32(6) protects`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the repeal, amendment or expiry ends` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Act, instrument or provision has been repealed or amended, or has expired`) THEN NOTHING
    ELSE (CONSIDER thing
            WHEN `the continued operation of a provision of a savings or transitional nature enacted or made by the Act, instrument or provision` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `the validating effect of a provision enacted or made by the Act, instrument or provision that validates anything that is or may otherwise be invalid` THEN JUST FALSE
            WHEN `something else section 32(6) protects` THEN NOTHING)

DECLARE `Proceeding within section 32(7)` IS ONE OF
    `a proceeding pursuant to an Act or law, of a judicial nature`
    `a proceeding pursuant to an Act or law, of an administrative nature`
    `a proceeding that is not pursuant to an Act or law`

-- src:416 | (7) In this section—
-- src:417 | legal proceeding includes any proceeding pursuant to an Act or law whether of a judicial or administrative nature.
@ref s 32(7) (src:416-417)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Proceeding within section 32(7)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a proceeding is a legal proceeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
        WHEN `a proceeding pursuant to an Act or law, of a judicial nature` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a proceeding pursuant to an Act or law, of an administrative nature` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a proceeding that is not pursuant to an Act or law` THEN NOTHING

§§ `33 -- Saving of administrative acts and instruments when provisions replaced`

-- Section 33(3): a provision is taken to have been replaced if repealed or superseded by a later provision dealing with the same matter,
-- whether in the same manner or not, and whether it deals only with the matter or with other matters also.
-- src:424 | (3) An Act or a legislative instrument, or provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, will be taken to have been replaced if it has been repealed or superseded by a later Act, instrument or provision that deals with the same matter (whether it deals with the matter in the same manner or not and whether it deals only with the matter or with other matters also).
@ref s 33(3) (src:424)
GIVEN `it has been repealed or superseded by a later Act, instrument or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later one deals with the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an Act, instrument or provision is taken to have been replaced` MEANS
    IF `it has been repealed or superseded by a later Act, instrument or provision` AND `the later one deals with the same matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:419 | (1) If an Act or a legislative instrument, or a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, is replaced, an administrative act done in accordance with it (as in force before it was replaced and not being an administrative act the effect of which was exhausted) will be regarded as an administrative act done for the purposes of the replacement Act, instrument or provision if it is not inconsistent with the Act, instrument or provision as in force after it is replaced.
@ref s 33(1) (src:419)
GIVEN `the provision has been replaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was done in accordance with the provision as in force before it was replaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effect of the administrative act was exhausted before the replacement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is inconsistent with the provision as in force after it is replaced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an administrative act done under a replaced provision is regarded as done for the purposes of the replacement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the provision has been replaced` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `the act was done in accordance with the provision as in force before it was replaced` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the effect of the administrative act was exhausted before the replacement` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the act is inconsistent with the provision as in force after it is replaced` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:420 | (2) If—
-- src:421 | (a) a legislative instrument or other instrument is in force under a provision of an Act; and
-- src:422 | (b) the Act, or the provision of the Act, is replaced by a subsequent Act or provision that contains or provides a power to make instruments to the same or similar effect,
-- src:423 | the instrument will, subject to the subsequent Act or provision, remain in force as if the subsequent Act or provision had been in force when the instrument was made and the instrument had been made under that Act or provision.
@ref s 33(2) (src:420-423)
GIVEN `the instrument is in force under a provision of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Act or provision has been replaced by a subsequent Act or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent one contains or provides a power to make instruments to the same or similar effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the instrument remains in force as if made under the subsequent Act or provision` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is in force under a provision of an Act`
       AND `the Act or provision has been replaced by a subsequent Act or provision`
       AND `the subsequent one contains or provides a power to make instruments to the same or similar effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `34 -- Amendment or repeal of Act in session in which it was passed`

-- src:426 | An Act may be amended or repealed in the session of Parliament in which it was passed.
@ref s 34 (src:426)
`an Act may be amended or repealed in the session of Parliament in which it was passed` MEANS JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Thing a reference to a provision extends to` IS ONE OF
    `a part of a provision`
    `a provision to be inserted into another Act by the Act`
    `something else a reference to a provision extends to`

-- src:379 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (3), a reference to a provision of an Act extends to—
-- src:380 | (a) a part of a provision; and
-- src:381 | (b) a provision to be inserted into another Act by the Act.
@ref s 27(4) (src:379-381)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a reference to a provision extends to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to a provision of an Act extends to this for the purposes of section 27(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `a part of a provision` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a provision to be inserted into another Act by the Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `something else a reference to a provision extends to` THEN NOTHING

§§ `Tests`

#ASSERT `an Act or legislative instrument may include a provision specifying a day on which it expires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 31
#ASSERT `a provision under a heading amends what the heading specifies` `an Act` `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision under a heading amends what the heading specifies` `an Act` `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by another authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision under a heading amends what the heading specifies` `a legislative instrument` `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by the same authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision under a heading amends what the heading specifies` `a legislative instrument` `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified legislative instrument made by another authority` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a provision under a heading amends what the heading specifies` `a legislative instrument` `a heading referring to the amendment of a specified Act` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 32(2)
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` TRUE `reviving anything not in force or existing at that time` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` TRUE `the previous operation of the Act, instrument or provision, or anything duly done or suffered under it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` TRUE `any direct amendments made by the Act, instrument or provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` TRUE `a right, interest, title, power or privilege created, acquired, accrued, established or exercisable, or a status or capacity existing, under it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` TRUE `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment, imposed, created or incurred, or liable to be, under it` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` TRUE `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right or such a duty or penalty` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` TRUE `something else a repeal, amendment or expiry might touch` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry affects` FALSE `reviving anything not in force or existing at that time` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry ends` TRUE `the continued operation of a provision of a savings or transitional nature enacted or made by the Act, instrument or provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry ends` TRUE `the validating effect of a provision enacted or made by the Act, instrument or provision that validates anything that is or may otherwise be invalid` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry ends` TRUE `something else section 32(6) protects` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the repeal, amendment or expiry ends` FALSE `something else section 32(6) protects` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 32(3) to (5), (7)
#ASSERT `it may be commenced, continued, enforced or imposed as if the Act had not been repealed, amended or expired` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy mentioned in section 32(2)(f)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it may be commenced, continued, enforced or imposed as if the Act had not been repealed, amended or expired` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment mentioned in section 32(2)(e)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it may be commenced, continued, enforced or imposed as if the Act had not been repealed, amended or expired` `any other proceeding or penalty` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the office, court, tribunal or body continues in existence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the office, court, tribunal or body continues in existence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the office, court, tribunal or body continues in existence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repealed, amended or expired provision continues in force for completing the act, matter or thing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the repealed, amended or expired provision continues in force for completing the act, matter or thing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repealed, amended or expired provision continues in force for completing the act, matter or thing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a proceeding is a legal proceeding` `a proceeding pursuant to an Act or law, of a judicial nature` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a proceeding is a legal proceeding` `a proceeding pursuant to an Act or law, of an administrative nature` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a proceeding is a legal proceeding` `a proceeding that is not pursuant to an Act or law` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 33
#ASSERT `an Act, instrument or provision is taken to have been replaced` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act, instrument or provision is taken to have been replaced` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act, instrument or provision is taken to have been replaced` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an administrative act done under a replaced provision is regarded as done for the purposes of the replacement` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an administrative act done under a replaced provision is regarded as done for the purposes of the replacement` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an administrative act done under a replaced provision is regarded as done for the purposes of the replacement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an administrative act done under a replaced provision is regarded as done for the purposes of the replacement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an administrative act done under a replaced provision is regarded as done for the purposes of the replacement` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the instrument remains in force as if made under the subsequent Act or provision` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the instrument remains in force as if made under the subsequent Act or provision` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the instrument remains in force as if made under the subsequent Act or provision` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the instrument remains in force as if made under the subsequent Act or provision` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a reference to a provision of an Act extends to this for the purposes of section 27(3)` `a part of a provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a provision of an Act extends to this for the purposes of section 27(3)` `a provision to be inserted into another Act by the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to a provision of an Act extends to this for the purposes of section 27(3)` `something else a reference to a provision extends to` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act may be amended or repealed in the session of Parliament in which it was passed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
